// The shape of a logged event, replacing Dogwood's default event schema.
//
// The default declares `pin callerPrincipal ... = principal` on every kind,
// which is a universal symmetric pin: every temporal leaf is then evaluated
// over the slice of the trace belonging to the requesting principal, and the
// pin is appended to every predicate whether or not the policy wrote it. Both
// halves are wrong here. The cap is on the order, not on whoever paid, and an
// event without `callerPrincipal` silently matches no pinned predicate, which
// measured under the default schema makes the rolling cap permit everything.
//
// Only `request` is declared, because a payment is logged exactly one way. An
// event of an undeclared kind yields no verdict, which `DogwoodCli.replay`
// refuses; an undeclared *field* on a declared kind is accepted in silence, so
// the fields below are the ones a predicate may correlate on and no more.
decision event <A>::request {
    ...inputs(A),
    // What scopes the window to one order; `pay.dw` correlates on it.
    callerResource: resourceType(A),
}
